      "editorial": {
        "en": {
          "why_it_matters": "The draw is the collision of three very different rhythmic and improvisational worlds under one festival roof: O'Farrill's large-ensemble Afro-Latin writing, Melford's exploratory piano language, and Braimah's percussion-centered work with The Hands of Time. That makes the current lineup more than a sampler of good jazz names; it sketches a genuinely broad map of how composition, groove and improvisation can relate in contemporary jazz. The remaining TBA artists could strengthen the case further, but the announced core already clears the RADAR threshold on its own.",
          "trip_verdict": "Actively make room for one of the two festival nights if a New York trip overlaps, and consider the second night once the remaining lineup is announced. The two-night format and recurring festival structure give enough flexibility that it should complement, not displace, a truly singular premiere, farewell or one-off elsewhere in the itinerary.",
